INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41898, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It pains me to ask of such things... The Blackroot were once our friends and dearest allies. As much as it hurts to look upon familiar faces and see friends, it is good to know they are now free from the evil that gripped their hearts. You have done the Timbermaw proud, and for that, you shall be rewarded friend.', 0),
(41899, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'More of the corruption has been cleansed. Each Blackroot that is slain is another step closer to having our race be pure of the vile taint that has cursed us so gravely. The Timbermaw is thankful for your efforts.', 0),
(41907, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah yes, these trinkets have faired well, spared from the flame. I must thank you for all that you have done outsider. Without your help, these surely would have been destroyed. I can only offer you a paltry reward, I just hope it is enough to convey my thanks.', 0),
(41908, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Unrefined and primitive, but undoubtedly potent. $N, your selfless actions of today will not be forgotten. The villagers will hear from this, that I will make sure. Should you find more, do not hesitate to bring them to me.', 0),
(41909, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Heghala\'s beady eyes widen, if not by much. His agape mouth looks almost terrifying, as he bares his two rows of teeth.>$B$BPoresh Toralar! Blessed be the Twisting Nether! What you have brought us is breathtaking, the proper words to show our gratitude escape me. $N, your name shall be known by every Moro\'gai, from this day forward till the end of time.', 0),
(41910, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Father sent you? How unlikely of him to relegate a foreigner to me, but truth be told he hasn\'t been exactly himself lately. The betrayal is deeply seated, the Elder was a well-loved figure within the tribe, second only to my father. Which is exactly what makes his actions all the more despicable.', 0),
(41911, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How barbaric. Tooru, how could you?! He was an aspiring hunter, his heart full of noble aspirations. To Nar\'lan, he was like a younger brother…$B$BI had thought after escaping from our dying homeworld, we\'d be safe from dangers, atleast for a while. How naive of me, you might say, and you may even be right. Nar\'lan knew the risks he\'d had to face, as he told me the night he left the village. His resolve was admirable. Today, the Moro\'gai have lost a great hunter and an even greater friend.', 0),
(41912, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is sacrilegious! What have they done to this crystal?!', 0),
(41913, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These will suffice, you have proven your usefulness even as a Parash\'ka. The chieftain\'s trust in you is more than peculiar, yet I trust his decision nonetheless. Now then, let us uncover what dark magic was cast upon this crystal.', 0),
(41914, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Fallen Ones were enslaved… no, they cooperated with the horned fiends you call Satyr? Unbelievable, after all that happened to our people on Draenor, how could Bhu\'robi spit on our traditions like that? The elder I know would\'ve never let the Draenethyst be defiled by foreign sorcerers. And if what is written in this letter is true… then my Father knows more than he dares to admit.', 0),
(41915, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'My son has matured a lot in these past years, it seems. Another regrettable thing I have failed to notice. He is becoming a man far sooner than I had given him credit for.$B$BAr’lia is right. The time of lamentation and idleness is over. We have not survived one genocide to succumb to another conducted by our own kin. Raise your arms, $N. We will silence this false prophet.', 0),
(41916, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I feel an aura of solemnity coming from you. Has it been done? Has this mistake of mine been corrected at last? $C, you have done a great deed for our people. Not only did you save us from damnation, but also showed us that the path we treaded for centuries is one the Moro\'gai shouldn\'t follow any longer. In a way, Bhu\'robi was right, the Draenei need to adapt, to ensure a new future for our people. One free of fear and instead filled with perseverance. If only he hadn\'t twisted the meaning of his own belief.', 0),
(41917, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Bhu\'robi might\'ve been stopped, but this ordeal is far from over. Like Father said, there are still many of the Fallon Ones out there that are now lost and it is our duty to bring them back into our fold. It is a grueling task and I fear this will not be the last day we lose loved ones, but that is exactly why we have to do everything we can to prevent that from happening. While I am yet inexperienced and in training still, I will support my father and the elders as much as possible.$B$BI have thought long about it, and while I still have much to accomplish here, your actions have instilled a fire in me that I haven\'t felt before. For all this time we have secluded ourselves at this coast, we held ourselves back and remained hidden as best we could. But this is not how I wish my life to go. But until I have ensured the security of the village, I cannot leave. So please take this crystal. Should you be in peril, hold it to the sky and I will aid you in battle. You can count on me, $N.', 0),
(41918, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, the silk I\'ve been desperately waiting for. Now that they are in my possession, I can weave them together with these bandages and infuse them with a speck of arcane magic. Our defenders will recover much more quickly now. Has Hara\'ne tasked you in retrieving this in her stead? That sly vixen. Don\'t get me wrong, she is not unreliable, but more so… resourceful. An unusual free spirit among us draenei, her wits and ingenuity are always refreshing and even more surprising at times. I was glad it was her who volunteered to gather the silk for our wounded.$B$BShould you ever return to the southern woods, please stop by her camp. I\'d rest more easily knowing someone would check for her well-being from time to time.', 0),
(41919, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hara\'ne is a thorough worker. When we still lived on Draenor, she brought all sorts of curious animals and plants to the village, many from which we developed either tasty meals, powerful cures or spiritual incense. I wouldn\'t be surprised if she used you as an excuse to explore the woods of this new and strange world and satiate her own curiosity. Please try not to feel disheartened by it.', 0),
(41920, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is that Maghan\'s cargo? How relieved I am to know he is safe and sound. I hadn\'t heard from him in hours and grew concerned about his health and safety. It is shameful to say, but the tribe is not united anymore, and many of our deserted kin have begun acting violently. While we have to protect our lives, they are still old friends and loved ones we had survived the exodus of Draenor with. This whole disaster is just too much to bear and I wish for it to end as soon as possible.$B$BExcuse me, that was uncalled for. Thank you for helping Maghan; and please, make yourself at home.', 0),
(41921, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What are you saying? You have been sent here by another draenei, a riftwalker no less?!', 0),
(41922, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A projection crystal... from another draenei?! Please, hand it to me quickly!', 0),
(41944, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Meat! And heaps of it, too! Parash’ka, who set you up for this? Or did you do it on your own volition? Either way, it hardly matters to me. With a supply like this, our defenders will have the strength to repel those heretics for days to come! A reward is needed for your actions. Here, a traditional draeneic recipe, altered to fit the cuisine of this new world.', 0),
(41945, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hm, I am surprised. You listened well and brought exemplary brains. The way their juices are dripping on the floor…$B$B<Fena Ma’dar is salivating at the sight of the grey matter inside your hands. With a swift movement, she snatches them out of your hand and starts chomping on them. Liquid, blood and bits fall to the floor.>$B$BI can’t get enough of this savoury taste, the slick surface, the gooey texture! It is simply wonderful! You remedied your mistake, young one. Atleast you are responsible when it comes to consequences caused by your actions. Either way, don’t cause any more ruckus around here!', 0),
(41946, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That was a close one. Let us hope this will teach them to not come here again. I thank you endlessly for saving my life and my dear farm. You see, the earth on this coast has unique properties that make it difficult to grow crops. On top of it, the flora of your world is still difficult for me to fully grasp, even after all the time we have been here. Still, I want to reward you for your good deed. Take it, they are homegrown!', 0),
(41947, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So the wretch has met its end? Excellent. Twenty three of our people did this monster maul during his last rampage. With him gone, we can rest a bit more easily now.', 0),
(41948, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, the nuisance of the south has been dealt with. These bearfolk elude me. Not long ago, they kept to themselves, barely engaging with the village, until they started acting violent and aggressive. It happened roughly around the same time that traitor Bhu’robi left the village. I hope there is no connection between the two…', 0),
(41949, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent display, Parash’ka. You are a true ally to the draenei, the real draenei. Don’t celebrate too soon, however. There is still much to be done.', 0),
(41950, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'More of those despicable crystals. I feel such anger inside me laying eyes upon this defilement of our sacred draenethyst. Tainted, broken and sullied. Whatever they’ve done with it is unforgivable!', 0),
(41951, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is true that I know a bit more about these crates, but it has been quite some time since I last saw them in person.', 0),
(41952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So it was the bearfolk who were acting as laymen between the hoofed fiends and the Fallen Ones. You are saying they tried delivering the crystals to the large cave up the hills towards the auburn cliffs? I have heard the network of tunnels beneath the mountain is their sacred hideout. A foreboding prospect.', 0),
(41968, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Bulrok Cloudhoof takes his time inspecting the horns, tapping his finger upon the surface of the bone with curiosity.>$B$BI believe this is what I am looking for, you have done well.$B$B<The arrogant tauren lets a smirk cross his face.>$B$BHere, take this as a token of thanks from the Cloudhoof tribe.', 0),
(41970, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, it is as I feared...$B$B<Torgan the Wise takes a moment, his face filled with sorrow, and dread.>$B$BMay their spirits pass peacefully to their ancestors. I do hope they met a quick, and merciful end. These poor individuals were only travelling here to celebrate, and now have only found brutality.', 0),
(41972, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Brave Wildheart inspects the letter, opening it, before gazing it over with a curious tone, the building rage and displeasure can be seen upon his features, all before a heavy snort could be heard.>$B$BThat road has always been dangerous, but for such violence? I will be sure to speak with Elder Moonhoof himself. This matter will need to be investigated further, for we do not know who the real attacker is. The Draenei have never been so overtly aggressive.$B$BI will be sure to have any others travelling to the refuge be under the supervision and escort of our defenders.', 0),
(41973, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Gordnak inspects the letter, a smile crossing his face.>$B$BZalwan huh? Been a few months since I heard from him, shocked he\'s still alive with all that stuff going on in Tel\'Abim, no wonder he wants out.', 0),
(41974, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Gordnak takes his time to inspect the scale, watching it glimmer in the light, and radiate with magical energy.>$B$BIt would appear this is what I have come for. You have done well, here, take this coin, and a reward on my behalf.', 0),
(41975, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ahh, bout time! I knew I could count on that big lunk of a tauren! Oh, and count on you, of course!$B$BNow all I need to do is wait a few days and kick this stinkhole, you\'ve done me a huge solid kid. This money is going to buy me a whole new life. A life away from water pumps and blistering fingers. Take it easy!', 0),
(41990, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is it done? Great, now let’s not waste any more time here. I’ll secure the relics and meet up with Richard back in Moro’gai Village. Thank you again for your help, stranger. I appreciate it. Here, you can keep one of the treasures for yourself, as a token of appreciation by me.', 0),
(41991, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Kralt lets out a huff of breath, a sigh of relief, his features easing from their aged stress.>$B$BYou have eased my burdens outsider, and for that I must thank you. My stockpile grows for the coming hibernation.$B$BPlease, take this, as a sign to show you not all furbolg are lost in rage.', 0),
(41992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Even after being recovered, the youngest sibling was placed last. This is merely the outcome of one far too zealous to seek anything other than the Sun.', 0),
(41993, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Pride and hatred blinded them into cunning yet mischievous powers. They chose to embrace young Lo’sho’s darker side. An appealing thing the rebellious sibling may be when the world itself seems against you.$B$BThe flow is shifting. Warmth makes my fur tingle. An’she is with us once more.', 0),
(41994, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is done then. A grim day, but it does not matter. An’she’s warmth will embrace me come dawn.', 0),
(41995, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You pay blood with more bloodshed. Do not think this absolves you of your actions. But you at least had the conviction to right your wrong.', 0),
(41996, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So you managed to cull some of their numbers. Well, better than nothing. Worst comes to shove, I will just shove some silk in my ears..', 0),
(41997, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, I will take this to Innkeeper Warmbreeze. He has the perfect kimchi recipe for this meat, and I bet he still keeps some of that stiff drink his night elven friends gave alongside the recipe.', 0),
(41998, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What a beautiful blue, to be expected, I suppose. This whole area seems to favor this color.', 0),
(41999, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'While I cannot provide you with new clothing just yet, you may choose from these I crafted from the last batch I had.', 0),
(42000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I sense some tranquility to the south; your task was indeed a success.', 0),
(42001, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Stand back while I dabble in forces you cannot even begin to imagine.', 0),
(42010, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It may look like they were buried for eons, but don’t be fooled. The waters within have a magical property which causes them to rise upwards to the surface, so that they may embrace the moon’s light once more. With Winterspring’s heavy snow however, they never could emerge truly. In case you are interested further, Owl Wing Thicket was once called the Temple of Lura’valas and was a place for worship for the goddess Elune. I may have diminished my practices of faith to her, but I still abide by her grace and judgement.$B$BNow, now; enough chitchat from me. I will repair the runestone, and as a thanks to you, will allow you to use it to visit my humble abode whenever curiosity strikes you. Feel free, it is my way of showing gratitude.', 0),
(42011, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I must admit, I was wrong. This crystal is different, certainly not a draenethyst. The mystery carries on.', 0),
(42012, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your friend is bold, perhaps even a little dense. Yet a gift is a gift; I will welcome him the next time he comes. The crystal you took from the whelps is called a Starshard; it is the splinters of a meteor. There, mystery solved. Now, unless you have more draenethyst to offer, I will return to my duties.', 0),
(42013, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So they truly were aggressive? Odd, to say the least. Why would druids of all people attack first and ask questions later?', 0),
(42014, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good, the influence of Lo’sho is being dimmed; a task well done. Consider the Windhorn allowed to shadow my village for longer.', 0),
(42015, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Nature will take its course, and her body will return to dirt, as do all bodies. I pray Lo’sho saves her mind and lets her roam amongst the stars she once loved.', 0),
(42016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'With that, our tasks seem to have reached an end. You have done me and my people a good service. I will not forget this kindness.', 0),
(42017, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I was half expecting you to mock me with the heart of a kodo, yet perhaps I judged you too rashly.', 0),
(42018, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ashtotem sends a humorous gift. He was meant to discuss diplomacy and alliances with the Moonhoof. Yet he was refused entry and decided to gift me the heart of Moonhoof’s oldest friend, which he himself deemed an enemy now. How chaotic.', 0),
(42019, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You managed to find one. Good. Give it here and wait.', 0),
(42020, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '“A gift from my brother. You have traveled far and wide to get to me; you have my deepest gratitude. To think my older brother put so much trust in my dream—it pleases me. I will do this weapon great justice.”', 0),
(42042, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It pains me it had to come to this, but their delusions have brought them too far away from redemption. For the sake of nature and its inhabitants, they had to return to the cycle.', 0),
(42043, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Some look worse for wear, but none of them should truly be irreparable. Great work, $N. We will ensure that they arrive safely at Nighthaven, so that they can be properly archived once and for all. Thank you for your diligence, truly.', 0),
(42044, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Loganaar received my message? What a relief.', 0),
(42046, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fine feathers, you are better at this than I have anticipated.', 0),
(42047, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your job is done and mine begins. I must tidy up the place now.', 0),
(42048, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Groundstender Rainhorn’s complaints? You must be kidding. I explained our situation to that old woman several times. Alas, I will send her a young bull or two.', 0),
(42049, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Those of the Earthen Circle have deemed the shrines of Moonwhisper restless. And my aid is required to soothe them?', 0),
(42050, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I wonder if the Duke saw something in you. His words are not to be taken lightly. It is a great honor to be spoken to so reverently by the elements, especially one of such title. Speak to Lotka, your next quest awaits.', 0),
(42051, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done. With the help of water, the Earthen Ring and you, the elements rest. Knowing that their wrath is not yet required. The mortals of Moonwhisper Coast will face its turmoil with great conviction.', 0),
(42052, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It may seem mindless to many and to many it is. This hunt of dragons does not come simply at the whims of one orc’s sport. Where these dragons were once meant to protect, they now seek to destroy.', 0),
(42053, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Pick. One is my for the taking, yours is the other.', 0),
(42061, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, thank the Light.$B$BAstalor finally sent someone. Good. Very good. I was beginning to think he had… forgotten.$B$BAs you can see, everything here is proceeding exactly as planned. Perfectly, even. Nothing has gone wrong. At all.$B$BThe expedition force is… mostly intact. Entirely intact, really. I certainly did not lose most of it. That would be absurd.$B$BAnd even if I had, which I have not, the situation would still be well under control. Completely.$B$BStill. It is… reassuring that you are here now.$B$BMy mission here is of great importance to our house. Critical, in fact. I simply require a bit of… assistance.', 0),
(42062, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have seen it, I am certain. The corruption that grips this land. The twisted creatures that now call it home.$B$BThe Sentinels will not allow this suffering to continue. These shores are part of Kalimdor, and they will not be abandoned to darkness.$B$BBy oath and by duty, we will bring justice to this place. When the corruption is cleansed, peace will follow.', 0),
(42063, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'From Velaya? Oh… you have no idea how long I have been waiting for this.$B$BI was starting to think she had forgotten me. A girl can only wait so long, you know.$B$B<Irea’s smile brightens, the worry lifting from her face.>$B$BThank you, truly. This means more to me than you might think. I will have to write back to her soon. Very soon.$B$BIf you are staying the night, the first drink is on the house.', 0),
(42064, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good. This will keep us alive a while longer.$B$BDo not think this ends anything. The theft was not desperation - it was intent. They wanted to see how we would respond. Whether we were weak.$B$BNow they know better.$B$BThey will test us again. They always do. Wounded beasts grow bold when cornered. If we wait, they will gather, and they will come for us in the dark.$B$BNext time, we do not recover what was taken.$B$BNext time, we burn the hand that reaches for us.', 0),
(42065, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Forty heads.$B$BIt brings a measure of peace, seeing them laid out like that. Not enough, but some. We have only carved a dent in their numbers, nothing more.$B$BStill, it should give them pause. Fear lingers longer than pain, and they are not brave creatures when faced with open slaughter.$B$BWith luck, it will be enough to keep them from testing our encampment while we are still here.', 0),
(42066, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, these are potent.$B$BThe magic on them is still alive. Old, refined, dangerous. Otherworldly, even. And the craftsmanship… honestly, it is almost enough to make me nostalgic. Almost.$B$BYes, these are very much worth investigating. Possibly worth more than that, depending on who is asking.$B$BWell done, $C. You earned your keep.', 0),
(42067, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So… you actually found one.$B$BYes. This resonance. I can feel it even through the wards. The arcane pattern is unstable, but not chaotic. That is rare. Very rare.$B$BYou did well to survive long enough to bring it back. Many would not have.$B$BWith this shard, the draenethyst may finally reveal its purpose. Or confirm my fears about it. Either outcome is preferable to ignorance.$B$BRest now. I will begin the work immediately, and carefully.', 0),
(42068, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Our people have endured exile, betrayal, and slow decay, and still we stand. We will endure this as well. I believe that. I have to.$B$BThat said, belief alone will not carry us through what waits in that den. Pride has already cost us enough.$B$BI will admit this, if only once. I could use a steady hand at my side in this matter.', 0),
(42069, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What is this?$B$B<Andanil stares into the artifact you retrieved. His eyes linger too long, as if it is staring back.>$B$BThis is it?$B$BYes… of course it is. I see it now.$B$BThe magic is spent, drained dry, but there is no doubt. This is the source. This is what they found. Even emptied, it hums with purpose.$B$B<He lifts the object carefully, almost reverently, turning it in the light.>$B$BSuch precision. There is no waste here, no ornament for vanity’s sake. This is not elven craft.$B$BI have studied relics from every corner of our past. Highborne vaults. Pre-Sundering ruins. Nothing even approaches this. Whatever made it did not think like us. It did not feel like us. And whatever power once flowed through it was enough to drain trained arcanists in moments and leave them wandering husks.$B$BAnd still, I cannot shake the feeling that this is only a shell. A key, perhaps. Something meant to be used again.$B$BI must return to Alah’thalas at once.  Oh cousin… this time, I did not fail you.', 0),
(42072, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So they agreed to help. I must prepare something to thank them. When all of this is over, I will travel myself to Thunder Bluff to express my gratitude. Earthmother knows my father will not.', 0),
(42073, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you not said enough?', 0),
(42074, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So he has revealed to you the reasons for his actions. He sought your help and knows death is one of the endings he might expect for his mistakes. Enough of that for now, tell me of this relic, and this letter you found.', 0),
(42075, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That will do. Keep your allies close, you will certainly need them for what comes next.', 0),
(42076, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you, now it is finally time to leave this damned place and return to the home I have lost. Farewell, member of the Horde. May we never cross paths again.', 0),
(42077, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So this marks the end. Arch Druid Mothshroud is gone, and Ireth Moondancer is still alive. He meant to strike the moon out of the sky. And he almost did, were you not here to stop him. We must report this to my father, but before we do, I believe a reward is in order for all your valiant deeds.', 0),
(42078, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I understand. I am not sure I am deserving of this mercy, or whether I would have given it myself were the roles reserved. I will accept my punishment and leave this village behind. It is time for another to lead then. With the help of his newfound allies, you included, he will certainly do far better than I.', 0),
(42079, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have recovered this from the clutches of the demon that claimed the barrow den from the Grove of the Moon as home? Then, whatever lies on that paper is only for your eyes to see. Find a lone place and read it.', 0),
(42080, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A bit of both then, member of the Horde. To what do I owe this untimely aid?', 0),
(42081, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Torgan sent you, did he?$B$B<Elder Starstrider\'s features twist in annoyance>$B$BI suppose he is right. As much as I dislike our situation being aired out so openly.$B$B<The stubborn tauren snorts his displeasure of the situation, and how much Torgan may be correct.>$B$BWell, he is right, we do need help.', 0),
(42082, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Elder Starstrider gazes upon the feathers with aged and cold eyes, scanning them for imperfections>$B$BHmm... They are not in perfect condition, but they are good enough.', 0),
(42083, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Starstrider inspects the Rod for faults and damage, his eyes gazing over it with caution.>$B$BIt seems we have been spared a travesty. As crude as those little creatures are it would seem they have the foresight to not destroy everything in their clutches.', 0),
(42084, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It has been a while since I have had my hands on such a rare material. You have done well, I have not expected this from a guest in our lands.$B$BIt would seem I have much to learn from outsiders such as yourself.', 0),
(42085, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Our Ancestors have delivered us quite the omen, and yet I am unsure of what to make of it... Regardless, another festival has been concluded, and without your help, I would still be waiting for assistance from Moonhoof Village.$B$BI must reward you for your generosity outsider. Please, take this, on behalf of myself, and all of those in my tribe. May your travels be gentle, and the road ahead free from burden.', 0),
(42086, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah… yes.$B$B<Talanis carefully lifts one of the objects you recovered, turning it slowly in the light.>$B$BA child’s carving knife. See the worn handle? Used for years. Passed from hand to hand, perhaps. And this… a moon pendant. The silverwork is crude, but earnest. Likely made by someone learning their craft.$B$B<He exhales quietly.>$B$BThirty small pieces of a forgotten life. That is what you have brought me. History is not only written in great battles and kings, you know. Sometimes it survives in the things ordinary people carried with them each day. Thank you for retrieving these, $C. The naga may have taken the town, but they will not erase its memory.', 0),
(42087, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So… it truly remained there all this time.$B$B<Talanis studies the artifact in silence for a long moment.>$B$BRemarkable. The craftsmanship alone places it centuries before the founding of Zin-Azshari. And the lunar resonance… yes, I can feel it even now. This was no mere ceremonial piece. It was used. Studied. Revered. The priestesses of Elunaris must have trained beneath its light, learning to channel Elune’s blessing through it.$B$BYou have brought back more than a relic today. You have returned a fragment of our past that might otherwise have vanished with the temple itself.', 0),
(42088, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So it is done.$B$BI take no satisfaction in this. Still… if they had been left unchecked, more would have died. We will keep watch on the rest of their tribes. If this corruption spreads, we will know. Until then, Narvalis Point remains secure. That is what matters.', 0),
(42089, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thirty scales.$B$B<She turns one over in her gauntleted hand, inspecting the deep green sheen.>$B$BThese belonged to seasoned warriors. Killing this many will have been noticed among their ranks.$B$BGood.$B$BStill… their true leaders remain. And until they fall, the Tideblade will not abandon these ruins.', 0),
(42090, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Lady Serpentia… and Ta’jax as well.$B$B<For the first time, Silverstreak allows herself a small, satisfied nod.>$B$BGood. Very good.$B$BWithout them, the Tideblade will splinter into rival broods. Naga are not known for unity when strong leaders are absent. That gives us the advantage. The ruins of Nendis may finally know peace again.$B$BThe High Priestess should hear of it.', 0),
(42091, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Lady Serpentia and Ta’jax are dead?$B$BThose names were spoken often during the war against Illidan. Their warbands left scars along this coast that have not yet faded. If they have truly fallen, then one of the last shadows from that time has finally been lifted.$B$BNendis has been silent for far too long. With the naga driven out, the ruins may finally be reclaimed. Not quickly. Wounds like these take time to heal. But in time… our people will return. Homes will be rebuilt. Temples restored. The forests will hear our voices again.$B$BMoonwhisper Coast was once a place where the kaldorei lived in peace beneath Elune’s light. Perhaps, slowly, it may become so again.$B$BYou have helped make that future possible, $C. Know that the sentinels of Narvalis Point have my gratitude… and so do you.', 0),
(42092, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Starcaller is dead?$B$BGood. That removes the most immediate obstacle.$B$BThe blue dragonflight rarely commits to guarding something so aggressively unless it carries great arcane significance.$B$BA meteor saturated with arcane energy… and dragons circling it like vultures.$B$BYes. There is definitely more to this crater than a simple rock from the sky. With that drake gone, perhaps the others will grow less bold. Or perhaps they will become curious enough to reveal what they were truly protecting.$B$BEither way, you have given us an opportunity to learn the truth.$B$BAnd I very much intend to take it.', 0),
(42093, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, excellent feathers.$B$B<Elendon runs one of them between his fingers, testing its strength.>$B$BSee the structure along the spine? Flexible, but firm. That is exactly what we need. With these I can finish a proper batch of arrows. The sentinels will appreciate the difference the next time they loose a volley across the treeline.$B$BYou have my thanks, $C.', 0),
(42094, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So the grove has been quieted… for now.$B$BI hoped the corruption had not spread this far, but the signs are unmistakable. These druids no longer serve the balance of the wilds. Something has guided them down this path.$B$BThe Grove of the Sun on the Isle of Tyrandas may hold answers. One of my allies tends the groves there.$B$BSeek out Sister Mirallun. She watches the forest more closely than most. Tell her what you have seen.', 0),
(42095, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Grove of the Moon has fallen to them as well?$B$BI had feared as much.$B$BThe forest has been restless for many nights now. Roots twist where they should grow straight. Dreams drift through the groves where none should linger.$B$BThe corruption runs deeper than a single grove.', 0),
(42096, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done what was necessary.$B$BThe forest breathes a little easier already.$B$BBut the druids who began this corruption still remain… and one of them leads the others.', 0),
(42097, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Krothis has fallen…$B$BThe forest mourns when a keeper dies, even one who lost his way.$B$BWithout Krothis guiding them, the corrupted druids will scatter. Some may yet remember the teachings they abandoned.$B$BOthers will follow Mothshroud deeper into shadow.$B$BThis is not the end of the matter. If Mothshroud truly walks these lands again, then the groves face a danger older than most remember.$B$BBut for now, the forest breathes a little easier.$B$BYou have done well.', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(41898, 0, 0, 'Has the corruption been rooted out?', 0),
(41899, 0, 0, 'There can be no peace with the Blackroot, they have sought our destruction ever since they have turned to madness. If you wish to get into the good graces of the Timbermaw, perhaps you can fight them on our behalf. Gather ten of the totems they hold sacred, it is how I will track your deeds.', 0),
(41907, 0, 0, 'The legacy of my people must be maintained, even if their spirits now walk with the ancestors. Our history can not be lost.', 0),
(41908, 0, 0, 'Our demand for draenethyst remains high. My tribe retains much of its spirituality from Draenor, something we take great pride in. This, however, has its cost. The draenethyst needed for our ancient rituals is scarce and we can barely leave the village without taking heavy risks. It may sound selfish and unsustainable to you, but what are we without our traditions?$B$B$N, the creatures of the coast are drawn to the foreign crystals, not unlike us. Their power is alluring, so like moths drawn to a flame, they gravitate to this tempting energy. For every piece of draenethyst you find, I will tell my people of your deeds, you have my word.', 0),
(41909, 0, 0, 'Large crystal formations are strewn across the coast. Most of their power has already been drained, turning them to nothing more than a beautiful mirror glistening in the rising sun. Yet still, Draenethyst begins to form, in small, glowing clusters all throughout Moonwhisper. They are a rare sight, but all the more powerful in turn.$B$BIf by some miracle you should stumble across these formations and bring them to the village, our people would be immensly indebted to you.', 0),
(41910, 0, 0, 'Welcome to Moro\'gai Village, how can I aid you?', 0),
(41911, 0, 0, 'We don\'t know their motives, and from what Father had told me about their reasons, something isn\'t adding up. If they were simply discontent with our way of living, they would not resort to such violence.', 0),
(41912, 0, 0, 'What is it, Parash\'ka? Don\'t waste my precious time with your infantile curiosity.', 0),
(41913, 0, 0, 'Make haste, young fool. The solution to this enigma cannot be postponed.', 0),
(41914, 0, 0, 'You\'ve been gone for a long time. What could Master Ral\'pekta uncover?', 0),
(41915, 0, 0, '<The chieftain gazes into the horizon with a melancholic expression.>', 0),
(41916, 0, 0, 'The shadow of fear that Bhu\'robi has cast upon our people must stop or else he will be no different than the orcish horde of Draenor.', 0),
(41918, 0, 0, 'Hara\'ne has been gone for far too long. Just what is this reckless woman doing?', 0),
(41919, 0, 0, 'You again? What brings you to me?', 0),
(41920, 0, 0, 'Greetings, Parash\'ka. You look tired from your journeys. This coast is far out in the wilderness, barely do we get visitors besides our local tauren neighbours.', 0),
(41922, 0, 0, '$N, it is good to see you again in the Harborage. How can I assist you?', 0),
(41944, 0, 0, 'Denphar struggles with his farm and F\'eesh couldn\'t reel in a fish for two days now! If this continues, we won’t be able to defend ourselves anymore...', 0),
(41945, 0, 0, 'What are you gawking at me like that? Move!', 0),
(41946, 0, 0, 'They’re still coming!', 0),
(41947, 0, 0, 'I have to coordinate the defenders, so be quick about your business.', 0),
(41948, 0, 0, 'What is it?', 0),
(41949, 0, 0, 'I want their blood to paint this coast dark red.', 0),
(41950, 0, 0, 'You are back, did you find something in that red canyon?', 0),
(41951, 0, 0, 'It is not safe out here. If you’re not familiar with these woods, I suggest you seek shelter at our village to the north.', 0),
(41952, 0, 0, 'If there are more than two parties involved in Bhu’robi’s scheme, then what does that tell us about his allegiances - and moreover, his aspirations?', 0),
(41968, 0, 0, 'I am not looking to waste my time, if you cannot procure the horns, I will find another who can.', 0),
(41970, 0, 0, 'Do you bring news? Be it good or bad?', 0),
(41972, 0, 0, 'How can I help you?', 0),
(41973, 0, 0, 'Is there something you need?', 0),
(41974, 0, 0, 'I would advise caution, the large behemoths carry immeasurable strength.', 0),
(41975, 0, 0, 'Back so soon are you?', 0),
(41990, 0, 0, 'I know this is disgraceful, but I just can’t help it.', 0),
(41991, 0, 0, 'So many things to do. Time always marching on.', 0),
(41992, 0, 0, 'Speak no word of this to any villager. We must not incur the Elder’s attention.', 0),
(41993, 0, 0, 'His silence is deafening.', 0),
(41994, 0, 0, 'The ancestors must be allowed to rest.', 0),
(41995, 0, 0, 'My words and anger are wasted on you, murderer.', 0),
(41996, 0, 0, 'My eyes are growing weary.', 0),
(41997, 0, 0, 'My expectations are high; do not fail me, adventurer.', 0),
(41998, 0, 0, 'Before you return, I will have some of my tools ready, alongside some concoctions to test against the crystal.', 0),
(41999, 0, 0, 'I wonder what I should tailor first.', 0),
(42000, 0, 0, 'You would be doing a kind favor.', 0),
(42001, 0, 0, 'Do not underestimate the furbolgs.', 0),
(42010, 0, 0, 'Who do you think is responsible for the runestone to malfunction? If you ask me, it must’ve been those blue rascals near the lake. Their magic is so primitive, something had to go wrong eventually.', 0),
(42011, 0, 0, 'I have yet to finish all my experiments on the draenethyst, yet I am very eager to see the other one.', 0),
(42012, 0, 0, 'Speak, traveler.', 0),
(42013, 0, 0, 'The price for survival is high.', 0),
(42014, 0, 0, 'Serve them the justice of An’she.', 0),
(42015, 0, 0, 'She used to whisper the name of the stars to me.', 0),
(42016, 0, 0, 'Steel yourself, friend.', 0),
(42017, 0, 0, 'Do not fret, she is deemed an enemy to the village.', 0),
(42018, 0, 0, 'I did not summon any of you Horde whelps, so why is it you approach?', 0),
(42019, 0, 0, 'I could use a break.', 0),
(42020, 0, 0, 'Something I can do for you, friend?', 0),
(42042, 0, 0, 'Whatever they hold in higher regard than my father Cenarius, it must be immensely powerful.', 0),
(42043, 0, 0, 'Beware, unseen powers linger in your adversaries. It is best to heed caution.', 0),
(42046, 0, 0, 'Is the task proving to be more challenging than you expected?', 0),
(42047, 0, 0, 'Often it feels like taking care of a kindergarten rather than a resting place in these lands.', 0),
(42048, 0, 0, 'Why do you bother me?', 0),
(42049, 0, 0, 'Boldly, you have sought an audience.', 0),
(42050, 0, 0, 'You return unharmed.', 0),
(42051, 0, 0, 'I am listening.', 0),
(42052, 0, 0, 'Steel yourself. Only a few may walk the path of glory.', 0),
(42053, 0, 0, 'Tell me, what are you fighting for?', 0),
(42061, 0, 0, 'A friendly face? Here?', 0),
(42062, 0, 0, 'Welcome to Narvalis Point.', 0),
(42063, 0, 0, 'Greetings, friend.', 0),
(42064, 0, 0, 'They are always watching.', 0),
(42065, 0, 0, 'Beware their daggers.$B$BThey coat the blades in venom not born of this world. It burns cold in the blood. I have watched strong warriors fall to their knees from a scratch no deeper than a thorn.$B$BDo not trust your armor to save you. Do not trust your healers to mend you in time. Even they struggle against that poison.', 0),
(42066, 0, 0, 'The Highborne ghosts still think they are alive. They haunt the ruins, patrolling streets that no longer exist, guarding cities that fell centuries ago. In their minds, nothing has changed.$B$BThey will not part with their secrets willingly. Nor their artifacts. Expect resistance. Ferocious, stubborn, and very offended that you dare disturb their illusion.', 0),
(42067, 0, 0, 'Proceed with caution.$B$BThe Fallen Ones are not to be underestimated. They are reckless, but not foolish, and they fight with a cruelty born of desperation.$B$BDo not take them lightly. Many have died that way.', 0),
(42068, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(42069, 0, 0, 'Do not stray too far.$B$BThere is another Barrow Den farther north, within a druid grove. The druids there have made their feelings toward us very clear, and they were not welcoming.$B$BWhatever they guard is not meant for us, and I will not have you provoking another enemy while we are already stretched thin.$B$BStay away from that place.', 0),
(42072, 0, 0, 'Are you the bearer of good news?', 0),
(42074, 0, 0, 'Your audience with my father took more than I expected.', 0),
(42075, 0, 0, 'Alive, but is it by victory or cowardice?', 0),
(42076, 0, 0, 'How many have you gathered?', 0),
(42077, 0, 0, 'Whenever I send you on a task you somehow end up being gone longer than I expected. Tell me, have you found Moondancer?', 0),
(42078, 0, 0, 'I have felt his death. Does mine follow?', 0),
(42079, 0, 0, 'Back for more training?', 0),
(42080, 0, 0, 'Are you friend or foe? A bit of both then, member of the Horde. To what do I owe this untimely aid?', 0),
(42081, 0, 0, 'Yes, how is it that I can help you?', 0),
(42082, 0, 0, 'I must remind you, be gentle with the feathers when they are acquired, they are delicate!', 0),
(42083, 0, 0, 'Be wary of the Draenei, they are a cunning foe.', 0),
(42084, 0, 0, 'I suggest you prepare yourself, this will be no easy task.', 0),
(42085, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(42086, 0, 0, 'Take care while you search the ruins. Even the smallest relic may hold a story worth remembering.', 0),
(42087, 0, 0, 'Now, the maddened druids and their lackeys walk in these once sacred halls. Be wary.', 0),
(42088, 0, 0, 'Tauren are formidable opponents. Their strength alone is enough to shatter shields and bones alike. Do not let their size fool you into thinking them slow.', 0),
(42089, 0, 0, 'Watch the water. Naga favor ambush. They will wait beneath the surface until you step too close to the shore. More than one patrol has learned that lesson the hard way.', 0),
(42090, 0, 0, 'Do not underestimate them.$B$BThese two commanded armies during Illidan’s campaign. They survived battles that slaughtered hundreds.$B$BCreatures like that do not fall easily.', 0),
(42091, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(42092, 0, 0, 'Starcaller will not fight like the creatures you are used to.$B$BBlue dragons wield arcane power as easily as most people breathe. Expect spells. Expect sudden bursts of energy that turn the air itself against you.$B$BAnd if the meteor truly empowers the creature…Then the fight may be more interesting than I anticipated.', 0),
(42093, 0, 0, 'Take care when approaching the hippogryphs. They are not hostile by nature, but they defend their nests fiercely. If one takes flight above you, keep your eyes open. They strike from the air faster than most people expect.', 0),
(42094, 0, 0, 'Be wary when dealing with druids who have abandoned balance.They still wield the same powers we do. The Dream still answers them… though it should not.$B$BThat alone makes them dangerous.', 0),
(42095, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(42096, 0, 0, 'Do not linger too long in Elun’aran.$B$BThe forest there no longer dreams peacefully. Something darker watches through its roots.', 0),
(42097, 0, 0, 'Krothis was once a keeper of the grove. Creatures like that do not fall easily and those who follow Mothshroud rarely fight alone.', 0);
